#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0289 expect=noViolation domain=TS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when TSVCDREF begins with 'CDISC' (e.g. 'CDISC CT') and TSVCDVER is not a valid published CDISC Controlled Terminology version (date).
#note "TSVCDREF='CDISC CT' names a CDISC terminology and TSVCDVER 2023-12-13 is a published CT package date -> no violation."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library published-ct-packages sdtmct-2023-10-26 sdtmct-2023-12-13
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSVCDREF type=Char label="Name of the Reference Terminology"
col TSVCDVER type=Char label="Parameter Value Code Version"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | CDISC CT | 2023-12-13
---
